# Two objects over RPC (#594's RPC half): the Worker asks the Ping, the
# Ping asks the Pong, and both replies come back.
{"path": "/relay"}
# The Pong asking the Ping back while the Ping waits on it is the refused
# cycle, over RPC as over fetch.
{"path": "/cycle"}
{"path": "/count"}
# An ask over the host's 32 MiB RPC limit is refused in beni before the
# call; a reply over it is Unreadable at the asker.
{"path": "/big-ask"}
{"path": "/big-reply"}
{"path": "/count"}
# A forwarded request meets the same cycle rule: the Pong forwards the
# Ping's request back while the Ping waits, and the Ping's chain refuses
# it with 508, Err Cycle at the Pong's forward.
{"path": "/forward-back"}
# The Pong throws while it holds the Ping's ask: the Ping sees Reset, the
# Pong is stopped, and its next event starts a new instance.
{"path": "/crash"}
{"path": "/count"}
